LYUNITS = 'DN s$^{-1}$'        / LateX units of the y axis                      LXLABEL = 'Wavelength ($\mu$m)' / LateX x-axis label                            LYLABEL = 'Count Rate (DN s$^{-1}$)' / LateX y-axis flux label                  LULABEL = '$\sigma$ (DN s$^{-1}$)' / LateX y-axis uncertainty label             CMB_NFL =                    8 / Number of spectra files combined               CMB_NAP =                    0 / Number of apertures combined                   CMB_STAT= 'robust weighted mean' / Combination statistic                        CMB_THSH=                    8 / Combination robust threshold (if used)         HISTORY Spextool FITS files contain an array of size                            HISTORY [nwaves,4,norders*naps]. The ith image (array[*,*,i]) contains          HISTORY the data for a single extraction aperture within an order such          HISTORY that, lambda=array[*,0,i], flux=array[*,1,i],                           HISTORY uncertainty=array[*,2,i],flag=array[*,3,i].  The zeroth image           HISTORY (array[*,*,0]) contains the data for the aperture in the order          HISTORY closest to the bottom of the detector that is closest to the            HISTORY bottom of the slit (i.e. also closest to the bottom of the              HISTORY detector).  Moving up the detector, the FITS array is filled in         HISTORY with subsequent extraction apertures.  If no orders have been           HISTORY deselected in the extraction process, the contents of the ith           HISTORY aperture in order j can be found as follows:                            HISTORY lambda=array[*,0,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                         HISTORY flux=array[*,1,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                           HISTORY uncertainty=array[*,2,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)],                    HISTORY flag=array[*,3,{j-min(orders)}*naps + (i-1)].                           HISTORY                                                                         